0,Cantares Mexicanos - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cantares_Mexicanos,"April 10, 2026 - The Cantares Mexicanos is a manuscript collection of Nahuatl songs or poems recorded in the 16th century. The 91 songs of the Cantares form the largest Nahuatl song collection, containing over half of all known traditional Nahuatl songs. It is currently located in the National Library of Mexico ...","Nahuatl, Highland Puebla",Uto-Aztecan
1,Sierra Puebla Nahuatl - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sierra_Puebla_Nahuatl,"December 3, 2025 - Sierra Puebla Nahuatl is one of the Eastern Peripheral varieties of Nahuatl, spoken by ethnic Nahua people in northwestern Puebla state in Mexico. The following description is that of the Sierra Puebla dialects: /t, n, l/ may also freely be heard as dental [t̪, n̪, l̪] among dialects.","Nahuatl, Highland Puebla",Uto-Aztecan
2,Uto-Aztecan languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uto-Aztecan_languages,"May 4, 2026 - In Mexico, they are spoken in the ... Luis Potosí, Hidalgo, Puebla, Veracruz, Morelos, State of Mexico, and in Mexico City. Classical Nahuatl (the language of the Aztecs) and its modern relatives, the Nahuan languages, are part of the Uto-Aztecan family....","Nahuatl, Highland Puebla",Uto-Aztecan
